r><td align="left">AF</td><td align="center">100</td><td align="center">233</td><td align="center">200</td><td align="center">0.384</td><td align="center">0.232</td><td align="center">0.152</td><td align="center">18.20</td><td align="center">93</td><td align="center">7</td></tr><tr><td align="left">AF<sub>aff</sub></td><td align="center">47</td><td align="center">118</td><td align="center">100</td><td align="center">0.386</td><td align="center">0.255</td><td align="center">0.131</td><td align="center">6.43</td><td align="center">33</td><td align="center">4</td></tr><tr><td align="left">RF<sub>L</sub></td><td align="center">50</td><td align="center">50</td><td align="center">50</td><td align="center">0.350</td><td align="center">0.260</td><td align="center">0.090</td><td align="center">1.19</td><td align="center">9</td><td align="center">5</td></tr><tr><td align="left">AF<sub>L</sub></td><td align="center">50</td><td align="center">110</td><td align="center">100</td><td align="center">0.373</td><td align="center">0.255</td><td align="center">0.118</td><td align="center">5.35</td><td align="center">27</td><td align="center">4</td></tr><tr><td align="left">SF</td><td align="center">100</td><td align="center">100</td><td align="center">100</td><td align="center">0.365</td><td align="center">0.255</td><td align="center">0.111</td><td align="center">5.66</td><td align="center">29</td><td align="center">4</td></tr><tr><td align="left">SF<sub>L</sub></td><td align="center">50</td><td align="center">50</td><td align="center">50</td><td align="center">0.360</td><td align="center">0.260</td><td align="center">0.100</td><td align="center">2.33</td><td align="center">11</td><td align="center">4</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><p><sup>a</sup>RF = One affected sib selected randomly from each family, AF = All affected sibs selected from each family, AF<sub>aff </sub>= All affected sibs selected from families with affected parents, RF<sub>L </sub>= One affected sib selected randomly from families with evidence for linkage, AF<sub>L </sub>= All affected sibs from families with evidence for linkage, SF = One affected sib with most evidence of allele-sharing from each family, SF<sub>L </sub>= One affected sib with most evidence of allele-sharing from families with evidence for linkage.</p></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></sec></back></article>